    <details><summary>Will it stop me sweating?</summary><p>No, and that’s on purpose. VURA works on the smell, not the sweat. Sweating is how your body cools down.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it sting after shaving?</summary><p>There’s no alcohol, and aloe vera keeps it gentle, so most people use it right after shaving. If your skin is cut or very irritated, wait a few hours.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Will it stain my clothes?</summary><p>No. It’s a clear mist that dries in seconds, so there are no white marks on dark clothes.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What does it smell like?</summary><p>Very lightly of rose. A trace of real rose oil is the only scent. There’s no synthetic perfume.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does one bottle last?</summary><p>About 2 months with 2–3 sprays on each underarm every day.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Does it contain aluminium?</summary><p>Fitkari (potassium alum) is a natural mineral that contains aluminium. VURA has no aluminium chlorohydrate, the sweat-blocking salt used in antiperspirants.</p></details>
    <details><summary>Can I pay cash on delivery?</summary><p>Yes. Choose cash on delivery at checkout for a ₹20 fee. Paying by UPI or card has no extra charge. Delivery is free either way.</p></details>
